@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #91AED1
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #1A2940
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #91AED1
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #4A302B
skinparam noteBorderColor #F1AD8A
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 45
title Contract outcomes — evidence required for a claim
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Identify exact operation / subject / context\nEvaluate current authority and applicable preconditions" as request
rectangle "Denied / invalid\nNo permitted consequential operation\nDo not expose unrelated private information" as deny #4A302B
rectangle "Eligible request\nEligibility alone is not completion" as eligible
rectangle "Actual attributable evidence\nAssess only the relevant effect and context" as evidence
rectangle "Confirmed required success\nClaim the matching postcondition\nApply frame to this operation" as success #17405A
rectangle "Definite failure / bounded partial / pending\nReport the specific known disposition\nDo not claim the success postcondition" as other #4A302B
rectangle "Unknown or contradictory effect\nDC-O38: reconcile same operation\nNo blind consequential repeat or assumed rollback" as unknown #4A302B
request --> deny : prerequisite not satisfied
request --> eligible : applicable prerequisites satisfied
eligible --> evidence : inspect outcome
evidence --> success : required effect established
evidence --> other : bounded evidence of another disposition
evidence --> unknown : required evidence unavailable / inconsistent
legend bottom
Interpretation guide, not a new execution algorithm, stored enum or retry policy.
Read-only operations and admission/cancellation requests have their own bounded success meaning.
endlegend

@enduml
